; fas9_tables.scr - step 9.1 (tables), F9.5 and the F9.27 gaps. Run it with
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_tables.scr
; on AutoCAD 2025's core (plain commands, no LISP).
;
; What the core can make of a table: the -TABLE command (columns, rows, width, height, insertion point). It has no
; in-place text editor (TABLEDIT picks a cell and then waits for one, the typed text is taken for a command), no
; -TABLESTYLE and no LISP/VBA, so a table made here has empty cells, and the text, formula, merge, border, fill,
; custom data and multiple-content branches of F9.5 are the ones doc/facit/12_tables.scr made by hand in the AutoCAD
; GUI (acad_<ver>_dxf_tables*.dxf, which HDxf's tests use as facit). The branches this file cannot make are
; "ej testat" in doc/plans/2026-10-27-fas-9-typer.md, Utfall 9.1: text/date/point/buffer values with a changed text
; (F9.5, F9.27), a table style with changed rows/borders (F9.5), a cell style of the user's (F9.5).
;
; What it does make: two tables of different size, which show AutoCAD's form of an EMPTY table (HDxf's add_table
; has to match it: -TABLE's rows are the data rows, AutoCAD adds the title and header row; the title row is merged;
; the table has NO extension dictionary and no TABLECONTENT/TABLEGEOMETRY — AutoCAD makes them when a cell has
; content), the same drawing with the first table moved (its proxy graphics and *T block follow) and with it
; erased (the BLOCK_RECORD *T goes, the style loses the table as a reactor: the B19 chain).
_.-TABLE
4
7
_W
35
_H
2
0,80
_.-TABLE
3
3
10,-20
;EXPECT ACAD_TABLE TABLESTYLE CELLSTYLEMAP
;SAVE table_empty
_.MOVE
_L

0,0
15,5
;SAVE table_empty moved
_.ERASE
_L

;SAVE table_empty erased
